<PRE>
IA #21-04, 4/4/08, REVISION TO IMPORT ALERT #21-04 "DETENTION WITHOUT PHYSICAL
EXAMINATION AND INCREASED SURVEILLANCE OF DRIED FRUITS" Attachment A 9/8/08,
Attachment B - 9/12/08

***This revision provides additional guidance, updates the product codes, and
includes Alert formatting changes.***"

     Alert language changes are bracketed by asterisks (***).

TYPE OF ALERT: Detention Without Physical Examination

(Note:    This import alert represents the Agency's current guidance to FDA
          field personnel regarding the manufacturer(s) and/or products(s)
          at issue.  It does not create or confer any rights for or on any
          person, and does not operate to bind FDA or the public).

PRODUCT:       Dried Preserved Fruits

PRODUCT
CODE:       ***20B[][][], 20H[][][], 20Q[][][]
               21B[][][], 21H[][][]
               22B[][][], 22H[][][]***

PROBLEM:       Filth
               Unsafe Color Additives
               Labeling
               Unsafe Food Additives
               Cyclamates
               Undeclared Saccharin

PAF:           FIL (Filth)
               FAD (Food Additives)
               COL (Colors in Foods and Cosmetics)
               LBL (Labeling)

PAC FOR
COLLECTION:    03819A, 09006A, 09006B

COUNTRY:       See Attachments

MANUFACTURER/
SHIPPER
& FEI# :       See Attachments

CHARGE:        For Detention Without Physical Examination charge:

               1.   Insect and/or Rodent Filth:

                    "The article is subject to refusal of admission
                    pursuant to Section 801(a)(3) in that it appears to
                    contain insect and/or rodent filth [Adulteration,
                    402(a)(3)]."

               2.   Artificial Sweeteners

                    a) Undeclared Saccharin:

                    "The article is subject to refusal of admission
                    pursuant to Section 801(a)(3) in that it fails to
                    declare the presence of saccharin as an added
                    ingredient [Misbranded 403(i)]."






               3.   Unsafe Food Additives

                    a) Cyclamates and/or Dulcin:

                    "The article is subject to refusal of admission
                    pursuant to Section 801(a)(3) in that it appears to
                    contain cyclamate and/or dulcin, an unsafe food
                    additive within the meaning of Section 409.
                    [Adulteration, 402(a)(2)(c)]"

               4.   Unsafe Color Additives:

                    "The article is subject to refusal of admission
                    pursuant to Section 801(a)(3) in that it appears to
                    contain color additives which are unsafe within the
                    meaning of 721(a). [Adulteration, 402(c)]"

OASIS CHARGE
CODE:          FILTHY
               SACCHARLBL
               CYCLAMATE
               DULCIN
               UNSAFE COL

RECOMMENDING
OFFICE:        Division of Import Operations & Policy (HFC-170)

REASON FOR
ALERT:    The history of detentions of dried preserved and/or sweetened
          plums from Hong Kong between March 1 and September 1, 1986,
          resulted in these products being detained without physical
          examination due to the presence of insect and/or rodent filth and
          non-nutritive sweeteners (saccharin and/or cyclamates).

          During FY '87 ORA conducted an import targeting project for
          preserved fruits. Samples of preserved, sweetened, dehydrated,
          candied, dried or salted fruits from Southeast Asian countries
          were collected. Analyses revealed non-permitted or undeclared
          color additives and non-nutritive sweeteners, a problem that
          appears to be pervasive in the industry.

          Dried preserved fruits from TAIWAN were found to contain non-
          nutritive sweeteners (saccharin and/or cyclamates, and one
          contained dulcin) and unapproved and/or undeclared color additives
          such as FD&C Yellow #5 (C.I. No. 19140 - tartrazine) FD&C Red #3
          C.I. No. 45430 - Erythrosine), and Carmoisine (C.I. No. 14720 -
          former ext. D&C Red #10).

          Samples of dried, preserved fruit from HONG KONG and the PEOPLES
          REPUBLIC OF CHINA were found to contain non-nutritive sweeteners,
          insect and/or rodent filth, and/or undeclared or non-permitted
          color additives.

          In addition to the above, examination of data from PODS, Import
          Detention System, and the import targeting project revealed
          violative samples from Thailand, Japan, Korea, and the
          Philippines; however, the number of violative samples was not
          enough to detain these countries without physical examination.

          THAILAND - Samples contained non-nutritive sweeteners
          (cyclamates and/or saccharin), undeclared color additives (FD&C
          Yellow #5 - Tartrazine (certifiable as FD&C Yellow No. 5), or
          Sunset Yellow FCF (certifiable as FD&C Yellow No. 6), and insect
          and/or rodent filth.


          JAPAN - Samples contained unapproved color additives, undeclared
          Tartrazine, and the non-nutritive sweetener saccharin).

          KOREA - Undeclared Tartrazine and the non-nutritive sweetener
          saccharin were found in one sample.

          PHILIPPINES - Samples contained the unapproved color additive
          Amaranth (C.I. No. 16185 - former FD&C Red #2) and undeclared
          Sunset Yellow FCF.

          Examples of types of dried preserved fruits which were found
          violative include: papaya, kumquats, prunes, mixed fruits, sugar
          palm fruit, sweet fruit, plum, mango, jujube fruit, mayom, lemon,
          grapes, olives, and tamarind.

          Dried fruit that has not been treated with preserving material
          (i.e., sweeteners, salt) are not subject to detention under this
          alert. These products should be treated in accordance with normal
          import procedures.

          Between August 1990 and January 1991, New York District collected
          31 samples of various dried, preserved fruit products from two
          manufacturers/shippers in Singapore. 7 of the 16 samples from Meng
          Chong Foodstuffs PTE.LTD were found to contain cyclamates while 12
          of the 15 samples from Kee Wee Hup Kee Manufacture PTE. LTD were
          found to contain cyclamates. Additionally, nine of the samplesfrom
          Kee Wee Hup Kee were found to contain undeclared saccharin.

GUIDANCE: ***Products other than dried and dried and preserved fruits should
          be covered under the guidance of Import Alert 45-07 for undeclared
          and/or non-permitted sweeteners.***

          This alert is intended to apply only to fruits that are dried and
          dried and preserved by adding sweeteners or salt.

          Fruit that is treated by drying alone is not subject to detention
          without physical examination under this alert and should be
          handled in accordance with normal import procedures.

          Districts may detain without physical examination shipments of
          dried preserved fruits from HONG KONG, PEOPLES REPUBLIC OF CHINA
          and TAIWAN except products from those ***manufacturers/***shippers
          identified in Attachment B of this alert.

          Districts may detain without physical examination shipments of
          dried preserved fruits from the manufacturers/shippers identified
          in Attachment A of this alert.

          Intensified coverage of dried fruits from other
          manufacturers/shippers for cyclamates, saccharin, insect/rodent
          filth, and color additives is indicated.

          If products are detained under this import alert and the importer
          or other responsible party submits documentation to demonstrate
          that the goods are not preserved by means other than drying, the
          products may be released.








          Continued coverage of dried fruits from Thailand, Japan, Korea,
          and the Philippines as well as other countries for insect/rodent
          filth, cyclamates, undeclared saccharin, and non-permitted color
          additives is indicated.  Surveillance of other preserved and/or
          sweetened fruits from these and other countries is indicated.


          For questions or issues concerning science, science policy, sample
          collection, analysis, preparation, or analytical methodology,
          contact the Division of Field Science at (301) 827-7605.


PRIORITIZATION
GUIDANCE:      I

FOI:           No purging is required

KEYWORDS:      filth, saccharin, dulcin, cyclamate, color additives

PREPARED BY:   Sammi L. Hadden, DIOP, (301)443-6553

DATE LOADED
INTO FIARS:    April 4, 2008


